   22	## Lifecycle guarantees
   23	
   24	These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` specify the hook features that follow against real behaviour.
   25	
   26	- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks, firing `onError` and then `afterSession`; a deployer can assume no user-input hooks, model response, tools, or tool rounds ran, and the turn was aborted before provider interaction ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40), [validated by: runs error cleanup in order when it throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L117)).
   27	- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
   28	- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
